Third-party code
----------------

`FormalProof/Definitions.lean` and `FormalProof/Basic.lean` are adapted from
`NMCode/CodingTheory.lean` and `N4Code/Definitions.lean` in

    Shenghao Yang, "n4code_lean_dev": a Lean 4 + mathlib formalization of
    Dong & Yang, "On Optimal Finite-Length Block Codes of Size Four for Binary
    Symmetric Channels", IEEE Trans. Inf. Theory 71(1):138-166, 2025.
    https://github.com/shhyang/n4code_lean_dev

which is distributed under the Apache License, Version 2.0.  The adaptation
covers the generic (paper-independent) layer only: binary words, bitwise XOR,
Hamming weight and distance, (n, M) codes with maximum-likelihood decoding
(`dRow`, `dCode`, `alpha`, `lambda`), and code equivalence, together with the
associated lemmas in `Basic.lean`.  Paper-specific material (the code classes,
the one/two-column comparison engines, the classification theorems) is *not*
copied.

The repository layout, documentation conventions (`PLAN.md`, `Notation.md`,
`CONSISTENCY.md`, `VERIFICATION.md`, `AGENTS.md`) and the verification
workflow are also modelled on that project.
